---
title: "Two DGX Sparks"
summary: "I want agents running continuously over my own codebase, tightening it for speed and hardening it for security, with no meter running — which means local models on hardware I own. Before I point anything at real code, I need to know whether I can measure it at all. So: two DGX Sparks, nine models, one deliberately broken Flask app, 22 criteria that drive the running application instead of inspecting its shape. The scoreboard is the least interesting output. The real one is forty-four harness bugs and zero confirmed model limitations — six scores in the final table were measuring my own code, not the models. This notebook is that work in order, wrong turns left in."
